# Coordination

Before implementation, name the boundary and claim exact writable paths through
repository MCP. Keep architecture-changing work single-lane; use disjoint
bounded implementation lanes and read-only auditors when parallelizing.

Modes:

AUDIT: read/search/query only; identify owner, violated law, duplicate
authority, earliest fact loss, smallest convergent repair, and falsifier.

IMPLEMENT: edit only after the boundary and writable paths are named. No scope
growth without new evidence.

VERIFY: adversarially inspect diff, generated artifacts, runtime behavior,
authorities, controls, differentials, and protocol exchanges.
